{"_id":"68a7362f8ec3d8323af1c570","nodeId":"vvTmjcWCVclOPY4f_5uB0","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# Sorting Algorithms\n\nSorting refers to arranging data in a particular format. Sorting algorithm specifies the way to arrange data in a particular order. Most common orders are in numerical or lexicographical order. The importance of sorting lies in the fact that data searching can be optimized to a very high level, if data is stored in a sorted manner.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Sorting Algorithms in Python","url":"https://realpython.com/sorting-algorithms-python/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae34b"},{"type":"article","title":"Python - Sorting Algorithms","url":"https://www.tutorialspoint.com/python_data_structure/python_sorting_algorithms.htm","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae34c"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/vvTmjcWCVclOPY4f_5uB0.md"}